{"kind":"request","text":"Close the kernel admission gaps: rests_on resolvability, explicit back-pressure, and the over-ceiling attachment path.","body":{"conditions":"Three admission behaviors the design states are absent from the kernel. First, shape-only admission includes rests_on references resolvable where in-log, but dangling in-log references sequence cleanly and every fold inherits the cleanup. Second, back-pressure is refuse-before-chaining, cheaply and explicitly, but the only overload behavior is the CAS retry cap, indistinguishable from contention. Third, above the genesis ceiling an attachment should degrade to a content-addressed hash reference with a locator hint, but the ceiling is a hard refusal with no reference path. Implement each, or narrow the contract by a ratified decision so the design and the kernel agree; add tests for all three refusal or degrade behaviors. Obtain independent exact-head review before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}